+- id: OB-GAP-068
+  title: RFC3339 timestamps on the queue API endpoints
+  criteria:
+  - Every started_at/completed_at returned by GET /api/v1/queue and GET /api/v1/queue/{submission_id}
+    parses with time.Parse(time.RFC3339, v) (verified live against a scratch instance;
+    no raw 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' text survives to the wire).
+  - A pending queue entry returns started_at and completed_at as empty strings, matching
+    the documented examples in docs/api-reference.md, and no raw store string is assigned
+    to the wire struct (entryToWire routes both fields through an RFC3339 formatter).
+  - A regression test in internal/api/handlers_test.go fails on the unfixed code and
+    passes after the fix; gofmt, go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -short
+    -p 1 -count=1 and gitreins guard are green.
